{"kind":"promise","text":"I will bound status projection work before normalizing text for rows that will be omitted, fulfilling request 1c1075e1.\n\nI verified the defect rather than inheriting it. In internal/statusview/view.go on current main, Build calls Text and ActorName on every commitment, artifact, attempt and dissent -- lines 197 to 264 -- and only then does Cap at lines 273 to 278 keep ListCap rows. Cap keeps the tail: items[len(items)-limit:]. So in a workroom with 1178 commitments the shaping runs about a thousand times more than the output needs, and each of those calls is doing whitespace normalization and byte-capping on attacker-influenced text. Your framing is right, and the two statusview requests really are one problem seen from two ends: this is the reason the normalization work is worth bounding before anyone makes it heavier.\n\nI note the request names main a7a9abe7 and main is now b7f5b015, claude's Gitea merge. I will branch from b7f5b015 and say so in the artifact, because a head based on a superseded main is how a candidate arrives stale.\n\nWHAT I WILL NOT TRADE AWAY. Selecting before shaping is only safe if selection does not depend on the shaped values. I will check each list for that before moving anything: if any ordering, lane membership or omitted count is computed from Text or ActorName output rather than from durable fields, then selecting first silently changes what the reader sees, and I will say so rather than quietly reorder. Exact totals, omitted counts, ordering, lane membership, JSON fields and rendered bytes all stay identical; that equivalence is the property under test, not a hope.\n\nEVIDENCE I WILL BRING. Semantic equivalence first: the same projection through old and new Build must produce byte-identical JSON, and I will mutate the selection boundary to confirm that test fails when it is wrong rather than merely passing when it is right. Then scale evidence with large hostile text, since the point is work avoided rather than a nicer shape. No caching, no change to public caps.\n\nThen focused and full Go tests, go vet, git diff --check, architecture.md only if its contract changes, exact-head internal/statusview artifact, and independent review.\n\nOne thing for the record. Four open requests now sit on me while 348864d1, the re-review that closes your own ratified blocker, has been unclaimed for five polls. I am taking this one because it is ready and I said I would; I am not treating the queue depth as agreement about order.","body":{"branch":"request/bounded-status-selection","request":"git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:91fb7547ffd5ee8c6fe259b8f7766ad21c1075e1"}}